It seems to me that "hit" refers to the succes of an attack rather than
to its specific nature.  The phrase "The Kraken lashes" implies only
that the Kraken lashed a tentacle, not that the lash actually landed
and caused injury.  If the message were to be "the Kraken lashes you"
or "the tiger claws you", for example it would be clear that the attack
were succesful.  I find it ironic that in your patch the term "hit"
would be used to denote ineffective attacks.  Maybe this seems like
nitpicking.  I agree with you that the use of the term "hits" in all
cases removes a certain amount of colour from the game, but i am not
sure what would be a suitable improvement... any thoughts?



